Abstract = {With the completion of the human genome and the growing number of
   diverse genomes being sequenced, a new age of evolutionary research is
   currently taking shape. The myriad of technological breakthroughs in
   biology that are leading to the unification of broad scientific fields
   such as molecular biology, biochemistry, physics, mathematics, and
   computer science are now known as systems biology. Here, I present an
   overview, with an emphasis on eukaryotes, of how the postgenomics era is
   adopting comparative approaches that go beyond comparisons among model
   organisms to shape the nascent field of evolutionary systems biology.},
